Implemented `Robot` in robot_name.py:

- `name` — lazy property; generates a random `[A-Z]{2}[0-9]{3}` name on first access and caches it.
- `reset()` — wipes the name (returns it to the pool) so the next access generates a fresh one.
- `_used_names` class-level set guarantees every currently-named robot is unique; generation retries on collision.

Verified with an inline script (no test files created): name starts unset, matches the required format, is stable across accesses, 20,000 robots all have unique names, and reset wipes + regenerates correctly while preserving global uniqueness. All checks passed.
